---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Suspension Development & Vehicle Dynamics | Too Fast To Race" description="Application-led Nitron and Penske suspension development, chassis tuning and vehicle dynamics consultancy for fast road, track day, Nürburgring and competition applications.">
  
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="stripe-accent"></span>
      <h1>Suspension <span class="text-green">Applications</span></h1>
      <p class="hero-subtitle">Real-world suspension development, chassis tuning and vehicle dynamics consultancy built around driver feedback, engineering understanding and motorsport experience.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Service: Suspension Setup -->
  <section id="suspension" class="service-detail">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="service-header">
        <span class="service-number">01</span>
        <h2>Suspension Development & Chassis Tuning</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="service-grid">
        <div class="service-content">
          <p class="lead">Fast cars are developed around confidence, predictability and meaningful driver feedback.</p>

          <p>Too Fast To Race specialises in Nitron and Penske suspension development for fast road, track day, Nürburgring and competition applications. Rather than simply supplying generic off-the-shelf suspension kits, we work directly with customers to develop suspension systems around the vehicle, tyre package, driver expectations and intended usage.</p>

          <p>Years of competitive driving and chassis development experience allow us to interpret subtle vehicle behaviour characteristics and translate them into meaningful setup direction. Ride quality, transient response, balance and tyre behaviour all communicate valuable information when understood correctly.</p>
          
          <h4>Areas Of Development:</h4>
          <ul class="service-list">
            <li>Suspension specification and setup direction</li>
            <li>Spring rate and damping philosophy</li>
            <li>Fast road and track day chassis tuning</li>
            <li>Nürburgring and competition applications</li>
            <li>Vehicle balance and tyre behaviour analysis</li>
            <li>Data-supported suspension development</li>
          </ul>
          
          <p>Where specialist damper servicing, rebuilds or dyno testing are required, we work closely with RaceShocks UK for technical support and damper analysis.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="service-features">
          <div class="feature-card">
            <h5>Fast Road Development</h5>
            <p>Suspension systems developed for genuine road compliance, confidence and driver engagement.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="feature-card">
            <h5>Track & Nürburgring</h5>
            <p>Balanced chassis setups focused on consistency, tyre control, stability and predictable limit behaviour.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="feature-card">
            <h5>Driver-Led Development</h5>
            <p>Combining subjective driver feedback with engineering understanding to identify and tune unwanted vehicle behaviour.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Service: Custom Valving -->
  <section id="valving" class="service-detail alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="service-header">
        <span class="service-number">02</span>
        <h2>Custom Valving & Damping Development</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="service-grid reverse">
        <div class="service-features">
          <div class="feature-card">
            <h5>Fast Road Compliance</h5>
            <p>Improved ride quality, surface compliance and driver confidence without sacrificing chassis control.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="feature-card">
            <h5>Track & Nürburgring Balance</h5>
            <p>Developing damping behaviour that maintains tyre control and consistency during sustained circuit use.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="feature-card">
            <h5>Vehicle Dynamics Development</h5>
            <p>Refining transient response, pitch control and chassis balance around the intended application and driver feel.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="service-content">
          <p class="lead">Effective damping development is about vehicle behaviour, not simply dyno graphs.</p>

          <p>Suspension feel is highly subjective. What gives one driver confidence may feel completely wrong to another. Too Fast To Race develops bespoke damping and valving specifications around the vehicle, tyre package, driver expectations and intended application rather than relying purely on generic baseline settings.</p>
          
          <p>Years of competitive driving and chassis development experience allow subtle vehicle behaviour characteristics to be identified and translated into meaningful damping direction. Ride quality, transient response, traction behaviour and chassis balance all communicate valuable information when understood correctly.</p>
          
          <h4>The Development Process:</h4>
          <ul class="service-list">
            <li>Consultation on vehicle usage and driver requirements</li>
            <li>Vehicle dynamics and chassis behaviour evaluation</li>
            <li>Damper dyno data interpretation</li>
            <li>Bespoke piston and shim stack specification</li>
            <li>Track testing and iterative refinement</li>
            <li>Setup recommendations and adjustment guidance</li>
          </ul>
          
          <p>Where required, bespoke valving implementation and dyno verification are supported through specialist technical partners including Nitron, Penske and RaceShocks UK to ensure the finished suspension package delivers the intended behaviour characteristics.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Service: Chassis Engineering -->
  <section id="chassis" class="service-detail">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="service-header">
        <span class="service-number">03</span>
        <h2>Chassis Engineering & Vehicle Dynamics</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="service-grid">
        <div class="service-content">
          <p class="lead">Suspension performance is ultimately governed by the complete vehicle system.</p>

          <p>A properly developed chassis is about far more than simply fitting quality dampers. Geometry, spring rates, tyre construction, weight distribution, roll stiffness, ride height and transient balance all influence how the vehicle behaves dynamically and how confidently the driver can exploit it.</p>
          
          <p>Too Fast To Race takes a holistic approach to chassis development, analysing how the complete vehicle behaves under braking, turn-in, traction loading and surface variation. The focus is on developing predictable, confidence-inspiring behaviour that genuinely suits the application and driver expectations.</p>
          
          <h4>Areas Of Chassis Development:</h4>
          <ul class="service-list">
            <li>Geometry evaluation and optimisation</li>
            <li>Corner weighting and balance adjustment</li>
            <li>Spring and anti-roll bar development</li>
            <li>Ride height and rake analysis</li>
            <li>Bump steer and steering response evaluation</li>
            <li>Caster, camber and toe optimisation</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="service-features">
          <div class="feature-card highlight">
            <h5>Vehicle Behaviour Analysis</h5>
            <p>Detailed evaluation of chassis behaviour, balance characteristics and driver feedback interpretation.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="feature-card">
            <h5>Setup & Development Days</h5>
            <p>Focused chassis development sessions combining setup changes, driver feedback and iterative refinement.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="feature-card">
            <h5>Long-Term Development</h5>
            <p>Ongoing suspension and chassis evolution programmes for serious track day and competition vehicles.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Service: Track Support -->
  <section id="track" class="service-detail alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="service-header">
        <span class="service-number">04</span>
        <h2>Trackside Development & Driver Feedback Analysis</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="service-grid reverse">
        <div class="service-features">
          <div class="feature-card">
            <h5>Trackside Chassis Tuning</h5>
            <p>Live suspension and chassis adjustments based on circuit conditions, tyre behaviour and driver feedback.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="feature-card">
            <h5>Data & Behaviour Analysis</h5>
            <p>Combining logged data with subjective vehicle feel to identify meaningful setup direction and development opportunities.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="feature-card">
            <h5>Development Support</h5>
            <p>Iterative setup refinement for drivers seeking improved confidence, predictability and usable performance.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="service-content">
          <p class="lead">Some of the most valuable suspension development happens at the circuit.</p>

          <p>Trackside testing allows subtle vehicle behaviour characteristics to be identified in real driving conditions where tyre loading, surface variation, braking stability and transient balance can all be properly evaluated.</p>
          
          <p>Too Fast To Race provides trackside chassis development and suspension tuning support for selected applications including Caterham race cars, lightweight track cars, Nürburgring-focused builds and fast road development programmes.</p>
          
          <h4>Trackside Development Support:</h4>
          <ul class="service-list">
            <li>Caterham Championship support</li>
            <li>Track day and testing programmes</li>
            <li>Hillclimb and sprint chassis development</li>
            <li>Driver feedback and setup interpretation</li>
            <li>Suspension adjustment direction</li>
            <li>Data-supported vehicle dynamics analysis</li>
          </ul>
          
          <p>Trackside work is focused on understanding how the vehicle behaves dynamically and using that information to refine the suspension package, chassis balance and driver confidence progressively over time.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="cta-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="cta-content">
        <h2>Discuss Your Suspension Project</h2>
        <p>Whether you need bespoke Nitron or Penske suspension specification, chassis development support or track-focused setup direction, Too Fast To Race provides consultation-led suspension development built around the individual vehicle and driver.</p>
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Discuss Your Car</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>

<style>
  /* Page Hero */
  .page-hero {
    padding: calc(80px + var(--space-xl)) 0 var(--space-lg);
    background: var(--tftr-darker);
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(92, 184, 92, 0.2);
  }

  .hero-subtitle {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--tftr-grey-light);
    max-width: 60ch;
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
  }

  /* Service Detail Sections */
  .service-detail {
    background: var(--tftr-black);
    scroll-margin-top: 80px;
  }

  .service-detail.alt {
    background: var(--tftr-darker);
  }

  .service-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: var(--space-md);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .service-number {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 5rem);
    color: var(--tftr-green);
    opacity: 0.3;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .service-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.5fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-xl);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .service-grid.reverse {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.5fr;
  }

  .service-grid.reverse .service-features {
    order: -1;
  }

  .service-content .lead {
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    color: var(--tftr-white);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .service-content p {
    color: var(--tftr-grey-light);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .service-content h4 {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    color: var(--tftr-green);
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .service-list {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .service-list li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--tftr-grey-light);
  }

  .service-list li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.6em;
    width: 8px;
    height: 2px;
    background: var(--tftr-green);
  }

  .service-features {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-md);
  }

  .feature-card {
    padding: var(--space-md);
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.02);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--tftr-green);
    transition: all 0.3s ease;
  }

  .feature-card:hover {
    background: rgba(92, 184, 92, 0.05);
    border-color: rgba(92, 184, 92, 0.3);
  }

  .feature-card.highlight {
    background: rgba(92, 184, 92, 0.1);
    border-color: var(--tftr-green);
  }

  .feature-card h5 {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);
  }

  .feature-card p {
    color: var(--tftr-grey-light);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* CTA Section */
  .cta-section {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--tftr-green-dark), var(--tftr-green));
    text-align: center;
  }

  .cta-content h2 {
    color: var(--tftr-black);
  }

  .cta-content p {
    color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.7);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    margin: var(--space-sm) auto var(--space-md);
    max-width: 50ch;
  }

  .cta-content .btn-primary {
    background: var(--tftr-black);
    color: var(--tftr-white);
  }

  .cta-content .btn-primary:hover {
    background: var(--tftr-darker);
  }

  /* Responsive */
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .service-grid,
    .service-grid.reverse {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .service-grid.reverse .service-features {
      order: 0;
    }

    .service-header {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: var(--space-xs);
    }
  }
</style>
